    ('292', "SPLIT THE SCREEN CODE (owner, 2026-11-25): AADPHUD::Tick is one function of about 3,300 lines at the compiler's size limit, so nothing more could be added and the compiler stops optimising it. Split into functions by subject, nothing changed in what it does. Done (c2369868, eight parts), compiled, not run. After the remote stands' ground vehicles (277 C), before its passengers (277 D).", 'about 1 hour', ['none'], '277', False),
    ('293', "SEATS ARE KNOWN TO EVERYONE (owner, 2026-11-25): in the apron bus, the coaches, taxis, aircraft and everywhere else, a seat the player sits on (or is going to) is never taken by anyone else, and people know each other's seats the same way, never two on one. In vehicles and aircraft cabins everyone takes the innermost free seat first (by the wall; in an aircraft by the fuselage), so the next can sit beside them, then the middle, then the aisle. Leaving is the reverse order: aisle first, row by row from the door, each waiting until the way is free, never all standing up and walking at once, so nobody passes through anybody. Apron bus, coaches and taxis with 277; the cabin when it comes (209).", 'with 277', ['none'], '277', False),
