    ('296', "WITH 277 (owner, 2026-11-25) - AIRCRAFT ASK FOR THEIR STAIRS AND BUS: if nothing came by itself (no stairs or no bus at the stand and none on its way), the aircraft's crew asks for it by radio; it is registered as a request with its time (seen by the player too), the ground crew takes it, and the crew checks back when it takes too long, more urgent each time. So no aircraft ever ends up unable to let its passengers off or on: a crew is taken from less urgent work, a spare vehicle is used, a broken or lost one is replaced, and somebody waiting on the steps never waits forever. The same for departures.", '15 min', ['people'], '277', False),
    ('297', "AFTER THE WEEKLY RESET, MONDAY 2026-11-30 (owner) - PEOPLE'S CLOSE-UP QUALITY (owner, 2026-11-25) - the person you talk to, and one invited into your office (nobody else in view there), in the best detail of all; and that same quality is the standard for everybody seen super close (the nearest layer of 205). Today passengers and crew are built at the MetaHuman crowd quality LOW (card hair, 2K skin lowered); the sources are kept, so they are built again at a close quality (Tools/make_metahumans.py refit, no cloud), strand hair only for the one talked to. First ONE person, beside the old one, measured (frames, memory, disk), then all 144 overnight, then the layers baked after it (rerun rule). Never a visible change in view: loaded before the talk camera gets close.", '45 min + one night PC', ['people'], '205', False),
    ('298', "IN THIS PUBLISH (owner) - THE CAMERA COMES CLOSE WHILE YOU TALK (owner, 2026-11-25) - talking with any person (passenger, crew, an invited one in the office) the camera gently zooms to them, first and third person: the whole face, neck and the top of the head in the picture, like a profile picture; gently back when it ends. Nothing in the way of it (walls, people, your own body), the eyes meet yours, a portrait effect the whole time you talk (like a phone's portrait mode: surroundings softly blurred, the person sharp; owner, 2026-11-25), gone when the talk is over, the subtitles and answers clear of the face; works on every screen shape, and a switch in the settings.", '20 min', ['people'], '', False),
    ('299', "WITH THE FIRST WIDE-BODY AIRCRAFT MODEL (owner asked 2026-11-25) - TALL PASSENGER STAIRS for the A330, 777, 787 and A350 (door sills about 4.4 to 5.1 m; the present ones reach 2.35 to 4.25 m): a longer vehicle from the present model, same controls, crew, IK, sounds and rules, blueprint for the owner's OK first; proven by measuring at a real wide-body's doors. Every flight is drawn as an A320 today, so nothing needs them yet.", '1-1.25 h', ['none'], '', False),
    ('300', "THIS PUBLISH (owner, 2026-11-25) - EVERY HIRED PERSON REALLY DOES THEIR JOB: for every role that can be hired, the whole way checked in the code and then in the run: hired, on shift, comes in 3D, is found for the task, goes there, does the work, goes home; the number needed is the number the game asks for; no role can be hired that does nothing without the game saying so; a check at start that logs every duty whose role has no people. Found by the owner's question: hired bus drivers never came in 3D.", '20-40 min', ['people'], '277 E', False),
    ('301', "THIS PUBLISH (owner, 2026-11-25) - ENOUGH CREW BY THEMSELVES: the game itself hires enough people for every job at the airport that needs somebody (all shifts), but low quality and without experience - cheap, slow, more mistakes - so hiring better ones pays off. New careers and the ones already played; only roles with a real job; the player can let them go and replace them; the hire list shows who they are.", '25-40 min', ['people'], '300', False),
    ('302', "THIS PUBLISH (owner, 2026-11-25) - THE TOWER AS NANITE: the control tower's curved walls, trim and desk flap (the last parts not Nanite; its 8,700 cubes and cylinders have been since 20 November) baked to Nanite meshes, the same look, collision and lighting inside. The glass stays as it is (see-through).", '12-19 min', ['gfx'], '', False),
