    ('309', "SMALL THINGS FROM THE RUNS OF 2026-11-25: the two P totems outside black; the departures board shows 15:43 before 10:40; the sign picture on the site not found; a yellow pole and a black one in the apron bus, pole tops ending in a point; feet up to 11 cm under the ground at single spots; Apron bus 3 'left open' each 20 s; 'THE BAR' mirrored; dark apron at night; hardly any dirt; passengers' trips 2.5-3.2 ms a frame. Not proven yet: the stairs and the bus on the remote apron (no aircraft came), spare vehicle, vehicle wash.", '30-60 min', ['people', 'gfx'], '', False),
    ('310', "AIRSIDE OPERATIONS VEHICLE (owner, 2026-11-26; was 'security vehicle') - the modern, beautiful car with the light bar (the one whose blue light bars become amber) is the AIRSIDE OPERATIONS car: its lettering (texture) reads AIRSIDE OPERATIONS (bilingual at Chablais like the signs), not security. Their job: drive the runway and taxiways (with tower clearance) checking for loose debris (FOD), damaged lights and the surface; bird and wildlife control - bird-scaring cartridges (bangers / screamers) from a launcher, recorded distress calls from the car's speaker. Hired as 'Airside operations officer' (role added 2026-11-26, no 3D job until this is built). Parked AIRSIDE in a marked Airside Operations bay (2-3 places, painted lines and a sign) against the terminal wall right by the staff door onto the apron, behind the stand safety lines - walk out, press E, drive. LIGHTS AMBER like the jetways' lamps, never blue: light-bar lenses photoreal amber glass, partly see-through; an amber flash animation lighting its surroundings through the lamp system, switched on and off by a key for the player and the same function for hired crew. Glow outline only when you are close and looking at it before getting in; none while you sit in it or drive. Security (lanes, fence, gates) stays its own role.", '?', ['none'], '', False),
    ('311', "NUMBER 1 OF THE NEXT BATCH (owner, 2026-11-26: 'a very important step') - MAINTENANCE INTO THE HANGARS IN 3D: today maintenance is only in the simulation (ADPMaint counts the 3 hangars as bays; the aircraft never moves). When an aircraft goes to maintenance a hired tug driver brings a pushback tug, connects the towbar as for a pushback, tows it along the taxiways to a free hangar, the doors open, the aircraft is placed exactly on the bay centre line and stop mark, the doors close; when done the tug tows it back to its stand. Amber beacons flash the whole time. AIRCRAFT LIGHTS AS IN REAL TOWING: a brake rider (mechanic) in the cockpit, aircraft on battery/APU power; red anti-collision beacon ON from hook-up to parked, navigation lights on at night/poor visibility, strobes OFF (runway only); wing walkers at the wingtips through the hangar doors; in the hangar: parking brake set, chocks in, beacon and all lights OFF, power off or ground power plugged in. THE BRAKE RIDER (hired crew) BOARDS FIRST: at a jetway stand the jetway connects and he walks in through it; at a remote stand a stair vehicle comes and he climbs in; then he switches the lights on. In the hangar he waits until a stair (a mobile stair kept in each hangar, at the side) is pushed to the door, then opens the door and climbs down; after maintenance the same way back in, and at the stand out via jetway or stairs. No cockpit/cabin yet: he walks in through the door and is held inside (hidden, linked to the aircraft) until he leaves through the door; the interiors come later. The player can do the same tow in the tug (same functions as the crew).", '?', ['field'], '', False),
    ('312', "OFFICE CALL WHEN BUSY (owner, 2026-11-26) - 'Call to my office' on someone busy: a notice right under the button (the row grows): '<name> is busy at the moment and will come to your office when free' with a live countdown (estimate from their job's time left); the same countdown on the normal game screen, lower right next to the other options (walking or at the desk, not in device mode), so you can be in the office before they knock. Native C++ HUD.", '?', ['people'], '', False),
