    ('314', "LATER (owner, 2026-11-26) - AIRCRAFT DELIVERY BY AIR: bought or leased aircraft arrive instantly for now (on a free stand at your base). Later each one is delivered as a real ferry flight: it lands on the runway and taxis to whichever gate or stand is free, then is yours. It lands no more than 15-20 minutes after you buy or lease it (game time), never days or weeks. Real approach: landing, taxi and turn-off lights on, strobes and beacon on, reverse thrust on the roll-out: the reverser sleeves really open, with sound and braking. Flaps, slats, spoilers (ground spoilers up on touchdown), ailerons, elevators and rudder move as on the real type (owner's OK 2026-11-26: these moving parts may be cut out of the Meshy models and animated). A water salute: two fire trucks, one each side of the taxiway, spray an arch with their roof turrets and the new aircraft taxis under it. It makes the news (a headline in the game's news). A countdown on the HUD, lower right where there is room (next to the office-call countdown of to-do 312; hidden while the tablet, phone, laptop or office PC is in use), titled 'Taking delivery: <type> <registration>', with how far away it is (km) and the minutes:seconds to touchdown from its real estimated time, reaching 0:00 at touchdown; native C++. AIRCRAFT SOUNDS (real CC0 recordings from Freesound, like the other sounds): engine start and spool-up, idle, taxi, take-off thrust, approach, touchdown, reverse thrust. Heard by distance and by walls (owner 2026-11-26): reverse thrust is always heard (the gates are near the runway), muffled indoors, full outdoors; spool-up is heard well at the gates, a little in the main hallway, not in the Grand Hall; take-off thrust is heard everywhere in the airport, muffled indoors and fading with distance; quieter details (taxi, idle) only near the aircraft.", '?', ['field'], '', False),
